# 4. Identifier Strategy

## 4.1 Primary Key Rule

Every entity SHALL use a generated identifier.

No entity SHALL use an auto-incrementing sequential integer as its public identifier.

```text
Buyer.id
Seller.id
Listing.id
Order.id
Review.id
```

Trace:

```text
REQ-ID-001
```

## 4.2 Identifier Properties

The identifier must:

* be generated by the application/database
* be unique
* not expose record position
* not allow simple sequential enumeration

The implementation may use a generated UUID-style identifier.

The exact identifier implementation is an implementation decision; the requirement is that it is generated and non-sequential.

