# 11. Listing State Machine

The listing lifecycle is:

```text
DRAFT
  │
  ▼
ACTIVE
  │
  ▼
SOLD_OUT
  │
  ▼
ARCHIVED
```

### States

| State      | Meaning                                                                      |
| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `DRAFT`    | Listing exists but is not available for purchase                             |
| `ACTIVE`   | Listing is available                                                         |
| `SOLD_OUT` | Listing is no longer available because available quantity has been exhausted |
| `ARCHIVED` | Listing has been removed from active marketplace availability                |

### Allowed Transitions

```text
DRAFT → ACTIVE
ACTIVE → SOLD_OUT
ACTIVE → ARCHIVED
SOLD_OUT → ARCHIVED
```

### Forbidden Transitions

```text
ARCHIVED → ACTIVE
ARCHIVED → DRAFT
SOLD_OUT → ACTIVE
```

The API/service layer SHALL validate lifecycle transitions.

The database SHALL enforce valid enum values.

Trace:

```text
REQ-LISTING-003
REQ-CONSTRAINT-005
```

