# 14. Order State Machine

The order lifecycle is:

```text
PENDING
   │
   ▼
CONFIRMED
   │
   ▼
COMPLETED
```

An order may also be cancelled from an appropriate pre-completion state:

```text
PENDING ──────► CANCELLED
CONFIRMED ────► CANCELLED
```

### States

| State       | Meaning                                  |
| ----------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `PENDING`   | Order has been created but not confirmed |
| `CONFIRMED` | Order has been accepted                  |
| `COMPLETED` | Purchase lifecycle has completed         |
| `CANCELLED` | Order will not be completed              |

### Allowed Transitions

```text
PENDING → CONFIRMED
PENDING → CANCELLED

CONFIRMED → COMPLETED
CONFIRMED → CANCELLED
```

### Forbidden Transitions

```text
COMPLETED → PENDING
COMPLETED → CONFIRMED
COMPLETED → CANCELLED
CANCELLED → PENDING
CANCELLED → CONFIRMED
CANCELLED → COMPLETED
```

The service layer SHALL enforce transition rules.

The database SHALL enforce valid state values.

Trace:

```text
REQ-ORDER-002
REQ-CONSTRAINT-005
```

